HW 011 :: What is this Sorcery?

1.1.1 Expressions

What is Lisp?

Expressions with lists in parenthese are called combinations. 

Nesting, in this context, is having elements of a combination be more combinations. When nesting, important to format for readability according to proper conventions.

1.1.2 Naming and the Environment

A name identifies a variable whose value is the object. Define key word used for naming.

Environment - memory that keeps track of the name-object pairs. 

Global environment - memory that keeps track of name-object pairs that can be accessed anywhere in the code. 

Define functions are not combinations as their purpose is to assign a value to a symbol/variable. This is an example of a special form.
